# Task 1 – Foundations of Cybersecurity

This is my work for Task 1 of the ApexPlanet Cybersecurity & Ethical Hacking Internship.

In this task, I worked with Kali Linux and practiced some basic cybersecurity, Linux, networking, and cryptography concepts.

## What I worked on

1. Cybersecurity Basics

I learned about the CIA Triad:

- "Confidentiality" – making sure information is only available to authorized people.
- "Integrity" – making sure information is not changed without permission.
- "Availability" – making sure systems and information are available when needed.

I also studied some common cybersecurity threats such as:

- Phishing
- Malware
- DDoS attacks
- SQL Injection
- Brute Force attacks
- Ransomware

Some common attack vectors covered were social engineering, wireless attacks, and insider threats.


