Linux Commands I Practiced

These are some of the basic Linux commands I used while working on Task 1.
Command
pwd - Shows where I am currently in the file system
ls - Shows files and folders 
cd - Moves to another directory 
mkdir - Creates a new folder 
touch - Creates a new file 
cat - Displays the contents of a file 
chmod - Changes file permissions 
whoami - Shows the current logged-in user 
ip addr - Shows IP and network information 
ping - Checks whether a host is reachable 
traceroute - Shows the path taken by network traffic 
sudo - Runs a command with administrator privileges 

